IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `P9-gate`

-- P9-art-80: Article 80, "Procedure for dealing with AI systems classified by the provider as non-high-risk in
-- application of Annex III" (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689, consolidated text of 27.7.2026; unchanged by the Omnibus).
-- Group General (Article 113, second paragraph: 2 August 2026). Each function takes `the date asked` first and the AI
-- system the provision is about; before the group applies, or where Article 111(2) saves the system, it answers
-- NOTHING (NOTHING-kind: limited by its own wording). JUST FALSE is the text's own "no": a "where" condition of the
-- paragraph that is not met (the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (b)). The market surveillance authority is an
-- official: it has no seat. What the Article means to the provider is asked in P9-seat-provider.l4.
-- Seam S1: the route by which the AI system is high-risk is an input (a system classified as non-high-risk under
-- Article 6(3) is a system listed in Annex III, so the route that matters is Article 6(2) and Annex III).
-- The consolidated text is a documentation tool with no legal effect: this is a rendering, not the official text.

§ `Article 80: the parties and the acts`

DECLARE `Art 80 party` IS ONE OF
    `Art 80 the market surveillance authority`
    `Art 80 the provider`

DECLARE `Art 80 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 80(1) carry out an evaluation of the AI system in respect of its classification as a high-risk AI system`
    `Art 80(2) require the provider to take all necessary actions and appropriate corrective action`
    `Art 80(3) inform the Commission and the other Member States of the results of the evaluation and of the actions required of the provider`
    `Art 80(4) ensure that all necessary action is taken to bring the AI system into compliance`
    `Art 80(5) ensure that all appropriate corrective action is taken in respect of all the AI systems concerned`

§ `Article 80(1): the market surveillance authority evaluates the classification`

-- src:1316 | 1. Where a market surveillance authority has sufficient reason to consider that an AI system classified by the provider as non-high-risk pursuant to Article 6(3) is indeed high-risk, the market surveillance authority shall carry out an evaluation of the AI system concerned in respect of its classification as a high-risk AI system based on the conditions set out in Article 6(3) and the Commission guidelines.
@ref Art 80(1) (src:1316)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the AI system was classified by its provider as non-high-risk pursuant to Article 6(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the market surveillance authority has sufficient reason to consider that the AI system is indeed high-risk` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 80(1) the market surveillance authority must carry out an evaluation of the classification` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies to the AI system` `the date asked` `the AI system`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application, and Article 111(2) may save the system; before that nothing is owed
    ELSE IF       `the AI system was classified by its provider as non-high-risk pursuant to Article 6(3)`
              AND `the market surveillance authority has sufficient reason to consider that the AI system is indeed high-risk`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a market surveillance authority has sufficient reason to consider that an AI system classified by the provider as non-high-risk pursuant to Article 6(3) is indeed high-risk" (a "where" condition that is not met)

@ref Art 80(1)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the AI system was classified by its provider as non-high-risk pursuant to Article 6(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the market surveillance authority has sufficient reason to consider that the AI system is indeed high-risk` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 80 party` `Art 80 act`
`Art 80(1) the duty of the market surveillance authority to evaluate the classification` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 80(1) the market surveillance authority must carry out an evaluation of the classification` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the AI system was classified by its provider as non-high-risk pursuant to Article 6(3)` `the market surveillance authority has sufficient reason to consider that the AI system is indeed high-risk`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        PARTY `Art 80 the market surveillance authority`
        MUST `Art 80(1) carry out an evaluation of the AI system in respect of its classification as a high-risk AI system`
        HENCE FULFILLED
    OTHERWISE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

