§ `Article 80(3): the market surveillance authority informs the Commission and the other Member States`

-- src:1318 | 3. Where the market surveillance authority considers that the use of the AI system concerned is not restricted to its national territory, it shall inform the Commission and the other Member States without undue delay of the results of the evaluation and of the actions which it has required the provider to take.
@ref Art 80(3) (src:1318)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the market surveillance authority considers that the use of the AI system concerned is not restricted to its national territory` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 80(3) the market surveillance authority must inform the Commission and the other Member States` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 80 to 98 and 101 and 112 the group General applies to the AI system` `the date asked` `the AI system`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 113 gives this provision its date of application, and Article 111(2) may save the system; before that nothing is owed
    ELSE IF `the market surveillance authority considers that the use of the AI system concerned is not restricted to its national territory`
         THEN JUST TRUE  -- "without undue delay": the text gives no number of days, so the duty has no deadline here
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the market surveillance authority considers that the use of the AI system concerned is not restricted to its national territory" (a "where" condition that is not met)

